---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PromptBlock from '../../components/PromptBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Customer Support cookbook · Pace"
  description="Customer support recipes for the Pace marketplace. Ticket triage in real time. Macro suggestions that match your voice. Escalation routing that respects who's on-call."
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook/customer-support"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-team-page-head">
      <a class="usecases-back-link" href="/cookbook">&larr; All cookbooks</a>
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">Customer Support cookbook</span>
      <h1>Customer Support</h1>
      <p class="usecases-team-page-tagline">Ticket triage in real time. Macro suggestions that match your voice. Escalation routing that respects who's on-call.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="usecases-team-page-body">
<article class="usecase-card usecase-card-marquee">
        <span class="usecase-card-badge">Marquee recipe</span>
        <h3>Real-time ticket triage with macro suggestion</h3>
        <p class="usecase-outcome">First-response time drops; quality stays high.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, API trigger fired by Intercom / Zendesk new-conversation webhook</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>ticket-triage</code>, <code>draft-response</code>, <code>customer-escalation</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (API trigger), Intercom/Zendesk + HubSpot connectors, plan mode for the draft, Slack escalation routing</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Every new ticket arrives with a pre-classified urgency, account context from HubSpot, and a draft response in the right tone for the customer segment. The agent reads the draft, makes a tweak, sends. First-response time drops; quality stays high.</p>

        <div class="usecase-setup">
          <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>
          <ol class="usecase-steps">
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Install the customer-support plugin</h5>
                <div class="usecase-step-actions">
                  <a class="usecase-step-btn" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=customer-support" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Install in Cowork &nearr;</a>
                  <code class="usecase-step-cmd">claude plugin install customer-support@pace</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Authorize Intercom (or Zendesk), HubSpot, Slack</h5>
                <p>Intercom / Zendesk for the ticket queue; HubSpot for account context; Slack for escalations.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Create an API-triggered routine</h5>
                <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>API</strong> trigger. Copy the URL + bearer token after save.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">4</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Wire Intercom (or Zendesk) to POST new conversations</h5>
                <p>In Intercom: <strong>Settings &rarr; Webhooks &rarr; New webhook</strong>, subscribe to "conversation.user.created", point at the routine URL with the bearer token. (Zendesk: <strong>Apps &amp; Integrations &rarr; Webhooks</strong>.) Then paste this routine prompt:</p>
                <PromptBlock prompt={`A new support ticket arrived. The conversation body is
in the incoming text field.

  1. Run ticket-triage to classify
     urgency (P1/P2/P3) and category.
  2. Pull the customer's account context from HubSpot
     (plan tier, recent activity, prior tickets).
  3. Run draft-response : tone
     should match the segment (enterprise / SMB / free).
     Park the draft in the conversation as a private note
     for the human agent to review before sending.
  4. If P1 OR enterprise tier: run
     customer-escalation to ping the
     on-call engineer in #support-escalations.`} />
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">5</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Send a test ticket to verify</h5>
                <p>Open a test conversation in Intercom from a sandbox account. Within ~30 seconds you should see a private note with the draft response. Once the format is right, every new ticket gets the same treatment.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Saturday on-call digest, no human babysitting</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekends 09:00 + 18:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>triage</code>, <code>escalate</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), Intercom + PagerDuty connectors, conditional escalation</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Twice on weekends, the routine sweeps Intercom. Routine tickets get auto-responses where the answer is in the knowledge base. The two or three that look real get summarized and paged to the on-call engineer with full context. The Sunday-night Slack thread no longer scrolls.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Turn five resolved tickets into one KB article, every week</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekly Friday 16:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>knowledge-base</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), Intercom + Notion connectors, sub-agent per theme</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Reads the week's resolved tickets, clusters them by theme, and for each theme with three or more occurrences, drafts a knowledge-base article. Plan mode stages the drafts in Notion; you publish the ones worth publishing. The KB grows from real volume instead of someone deciding what should be there in the abstract.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Customer context on every escalation, before engineering picks it up</h3>
        <p>When support escalates a ticket to engineering, a routine assembles the customer context first: account size, recent activity, open tickets, deal stage if any, prior escalations and their outcomes. Engineering doesn't ask support "is this customer important?"; the answer is already in the escalation.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, Intercom/Zendesk webhook on ticket-escalated</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>customer-escalation</code>, <code>customer-context</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (webhook), HubSpot + Intercom + Slack connectors</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="usecases-footer">
      <p>
        Have a customer support workflow that should live here? <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues/new">Open an issue</a> with the trigger, skills, and Claude features it uses; we'll fold it into the cookbook.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .usecases-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .usecases-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .usecases-lede strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Engineering callout above the TOC */
  .usecases-eng-callout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out-quart);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecases-eng-callout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  /* TOC grid */
  .usecases-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .usecases-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin: 0 6px var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .usecases-toc-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-toc-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .usecases-toc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .usecases-team {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .usecases-team-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-team-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-team-tagline {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecase-card-marquee {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 92%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .usecase-card-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecase-card-badge::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .usecase-card > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }
  /* Meta: small chip row at the bottom (was a big dl block at top) */
  .usecase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta > div {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .usecase-meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .usecase-meta dt::after {
    content: ":";
    margin-left: 1px;
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .usecase-meta dd code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .usecase-card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-footer {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-footer a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch a,
  .usecases-impeccable-when a,
  .usecases-team-tagline a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch code,
  .usecases-impeccable-when code,
  .usecases-team-tagline code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::before {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-right: var(--spacing-sm);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when p,
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecase-meta > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }

  /* Recipe card outcome-first ordering: prose before pills */
  .usecase-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 { order: 1; }
  .usecase-card-badge { order: 0; }
  .usecase-card > p { order: 2; }
  .usecase-card .usecase-meta { order: 3; margin-top: var(--spacing-md); }


  /* Outcome line at the top of every marquee card. Big bold one-liner
     that tells the visitor what they actually get before the prose. */
  .usecase-outcome {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
  }
  .usecase-setup-title {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .usecase-card > .usecase-setup,
  .usecase-card > .usecase-step-prompt,
  .usecase-card-marquee .usecase-setup { order: 4; }
</style>
